<title>UK: Sweden sets two bonds for total of 12.8 bln yen.</title>
<headline>Sweden sets two bonds for total of 12.8 bln yen.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following dual currency bond was announced by joint lead managers Morgan Stanley and Sanwa International (Europe).</p>
<p> BORROWER   KINGDOM OF SWEDEN</p>
<p> AMT    7.8 BLN YEN   COUPON    *4.00	MATURITY    18.DEC.98</p>
<p> TYPE   DUAL CURRENCY ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    18.DEC.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.50 PCT  REOFFER    =	   SPREAD	 =</p>
<p> NOTES     REDEMPTION IS IN U.S. DOLLARS OR YEN.</p>
<p>* * * * * * *</p>
<p>The following dual currency bond was announced by lead manager Morgan stanley.</p>
<p> AMT    5.0 BLN YEN   COUPON     7.00 PCT  MATURITY    24.DEC.97</p>
<p> TYPE   DUAL CURRENCY ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    24.DEC.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.00	REOFFER    =	   SPREAD	 =</p>
<p> NOTES     REDEMPTION IN NEW ZEALAND DOLLARS OR YEN.</p>
<p>* * * * * * *</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS:</p>
<p> MOODY	AA3	 LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA+	 DENOMS (K) 500</p>
<p> NOTES     ISSUED OFF AN EMTN PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
